{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n\\n#define DISTANCE_BLOCK_SIZE 256\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\\n    float block_distances[DISTANCE_BLOCK_SIZE];\\n    int has_nan = 0;\\n\\n    int i, j, x, y;\\n\\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\\n        labels[i] = -1;\\n        distances[i] = -1;\\n    }\\n\\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        Group g = groups[i];\\n\\n        for (int base = 0; base < g.length; ) {\\n            int block_count = g.length - base;\\n            if (block_count > DISTANCE_BLOCK_SIZE) {\\n                block_count = DISTANCE_BLOCK_SIZE;\\n            }\\n\\n            #pragma omp simd\\n            for (int t = 0; t < block_count; t++) {\\n                Point p = g.points[base + t];\\n                block_distances[t] = ((p.x - to_evaluate.x) * ((p.x - to_evaluate.x))) +\\n                                     ((p.y - to_evaluate.y) * (p.y - to_evaluate.y));\\n            }\\n\\n            for (int t = 0; t < block_count; t++) {\\n                float d = block_distances[t];\\n\\n                if (!has_nan && distances[k - 1] != -1 && d >= distances[k - 1]) {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n\\n                for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\\n                    if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\\n                        for (y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\\n                            distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\\n                            labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\\n                        }\\n\\n                        distances[x] = d;\\n                        labels[x] = g.label;\\n                        if (d != d) {\\n                            has_nan = 1;\\n                        }\\n\\n                        break;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            base += block_count;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\\n\\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\\n    int current_frequency = 1;\\n\\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n            }\\n\\n            current_frequency = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            current_frequency++;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    return most_frequent;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n\\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/knn.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"The distance block remains legally SIMD-vectorizable, while top-k insertion is dependency-constrained. When the candidate list contains no NaNs, a candidate at least as far as the current kth distance cannot enter the list, so rejecting it before the serial scan should preserve strict tie ordering while reducing dependent comparisons.\",\"notes\":\"Changed only src/knn.c. The original insertion scan is retained for NaN-containing candidate lists. No commands or tests were run.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Add a full-list cutoff before the dependent insertion scan; retain the existing SIMD distance loop and use the original scan whenever a NaN has entered the candidate list.\"]}"}}
